{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788220910,"nonce":"Wf6pl5U8wXpiSBpgYC1OxwgWUNc=","title":"map-view labels an odd-width building one cell off centre: _label_pass adds size/2 to a position that is already the centre","message":"Filed out of 2.5's fixture work (git-bug f7b6207), session 10. Cosmetic, but it\nputs a glyph on the wrong cell and a reader grading a render cannot tell a\nlabelling offset from a placement error.\n\n## What\n\n`baseviz/render.py`'s `_label_pass` centres a building's code at `at + size/2`.\nBut `map-dump` publishes `at = Thing.Position`, and for a building of ODD width\n\u003e= 3 `Thing.Position` IS ALREADY THE MIDDLE CELL — `GenAdj.OccupiedRect` builds\nthe rect around the position rather than from a corner. So the renderer adds half\na size that was never a corner offset, and the code lands one cell east of true\ncentre.\n\nConcretely: the 3x1 `ElectricStove` staged by 2.5's legibility fixture draws its\ncode one cell east of where the stove's centre actually is. The glyph still lands\nON the stove, which is why nobody has noticed, and why this is p3 rather than\nhigher — a 3-wide building is wide enough to absorb the error. A 3x1 building at\nthe edge of a rendered rect would put the code outside the building entirely.\n\n## Why it matters more than a cosmetic bug normally would\n\n2.5's whole value is being an INDEPENDENT SECOND READ of the same ground. A\nreader asked \"which cells is the stove on?\" grades against the published centre,\nso a labelling offset and a real placement error are indistinguishable from the\nimage. The fixture's question 4 exists precisely to check stove cells against the\npublished centre, so this defect sits directly on an acceptance path.\n\n## Expected behaviour\n\nThe code is drawn at the building's true centre, derived the same way the game\nderives it. Either stop adding `size/2` to a position that is already central, or\nhave `map-dump` publish a corner alongside `at` and have the renderer use that —\nbut pick one convention and make both ends cite it, the way `channel.alphabet`\nnow keys the two channels together (git-bug e6faa51).\n\n## Investigate existing code\n\n- `baseviz/render.py`, `_label_pass` — the `at + size/2` arithmetic.\n- `Source/AutoRimmer/MapDumpVerbs.cs` — what `at` actually is, and whether a\n  corner is available to publish.\n- `Verse/GenAdj.OccupiedRect` and `Thing.Position` in the decompiled tree —\n  confirm the centre semantics for odd and EVEN widths separately. An even-width\n  building has no middle cell and may well need the opposite treatment, which is\n  probably why the `size/2` was written in the first place. Do not fix the odd\n  case by breaking the even one.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A 3x1 building's code renders on its true centre cell.\n- An even-width building (2x2, 4x1) is checked in the same run and is not\n  regressed — state explicitly what the correct cell is for an even width, since\n  there is no middle one.\n- 2.5's fixture question 4 grades correctly against the published centre.","files":null}]}